1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,839
Day 52: Weight-Space Programming has a language model write

2
00:00:03,839 --> 00:00:07,677
another model's weights directly, with no gradient descent.

3
00:00:07,677 --> 00:00:10,019
We ran the official harness locally.

4
00:00:10,469 --> 00:00:13,529
The writer sees only ten ARC science questions,

5
00:00:13,529 --> 00:00:16,002
then writes a model's weights by hand.

6
00:00:16,002 --> 00:00:19,517
The paper reports 50.8 percent for Claude Opus's first

7
00:00:19,517 --> 00:00:20,233
generation.

8
00:00:20,683 --> 00:00:24,677
The harness launches Claude Code inside a bubblewrap sandbox

9
00:00:24,677 --> 00:00:27,805
that cannot see the test data, the home folder,

10
00:00:27,805 --> 00:00:29,402
or any host but the API.

11
00:00:29,852 --> 00:00:34,897
In 45 minutes, Opus wrote 4,071 lines of science facts and

12
00:00:34,897 --> 00:00:39,594
a retrieval procedure, using tensor operations with no

13
00:00:39,594 --> 00:00:40,464
branching.

14
00:00:40,914 --> 00:00:46,420
The harness then scored that model on the 3,530 held-out test

15
00:00:46,420 --> 00:00:47,323
questions.

16
00:00:47,773 --> 00:00:52,771
It scored 50.79 percent, matching the paper's 50.8.

17
00:00:52,771 --> 00:00:57,083
A smaller model written outside the harness,

18
00:00:57,083 --> 00:01:01,101
with only 155 facts, scored 31.3 percent.

